# Two decoupled first-order decays, nine decades apart in magnitude and three
# in rate — the smallest reproducer of lanl/bngsim#196.
#
#   S(0) = 1e-09, decays fast (kS = 10)
#   B(0) = 1e+01, decays slow (kB = 0.01)
#
# Analytical: S(t) = 1e-9*exp(-10*t), B(t) = 10*exp(-0.01*t).
#
# A single scalar atol cannot be a tolerance for both. At the default 1e-8, S is
# an order of magnitude BELOW its own absolute tolerance for the whole run, so
# it contributes nothing to the error test and its fast transient is resolved
# only by whatever step size B happens to ask for. At the ~1e-17 S needs, the
# step size collapses for a model that is otherwise trivial. Per-species
# tolerances (CVodeSVtolerances) are the only way to state both at once.
begin parameters
    1 kS  10.0   # Constant
    2 kB  0.01   # Constant
end parameters
begin species
    1 S()  1.0e-9
    2 B()  10.0
    3 Sd() 0
    4 Bd() 0
end species
begin reactions
    1 1 3 kS #_R1
    2 2 4 kB #_R2
end reactions
begin groups
    1 S_tot  1
    2 B_tot  2
end groups
